 "samples": [
  "Once upon a time there was a little boy named Ben. He was only three years old and he was a happy boy who he loved to ride around the park with his mom and dad and his new toy.\nOne day, Ben found a piece of yarn in his pocket. He thought it was so beautiful and he wanted to keep it for himself. He grabbed it and threw it around. It landed on the ground, and he did it!\nBen grabbed the yarn and started to bounce it, but instead he caught it. Suddenly, a big wind came and blew the yarn away from him! Ben was very sad and the yarn was gone. He cried and ran home very fast. Ben cried and cried, but the yarn was gone forever forever.",
  "Once upon a time, there was a reliable otter named Ollie. Ollie was very fast. He liked to run around the river with his friends. One day, Ollie saw a big, shiny thing on the ground. He thought it was a toy.\nThe big, red thing called a \"catch!\" Ollie was stuck in the mud. From that day on, Ollie and his friends played on the river together. They were very happy. Ollie and his friends were best friends forever.",
  "One day, a little boy named Tim went to the park. He saw a big tree with a branch. Tim thought, \"I want to climb the tree and climb the tree. But it is too high.\"\nTim said, \"I want to climb the tree. The tree is tall and tall. I want to climb it and reach it.\" Tim thought for a moment and said, \"Okay, let's climb the tree together.\"\nAs they climbed the tree, they saw a big tree. Tim said, \"Let's climb the tree and see what's behind the tree.\" So Tim climbed the tree and reached the tree. The tree was very happy.\nBut then, a big wind came and blew the tree away. Tim and Tim could not get the tree. The tree was now gone. Tim",
  "Once upon a time there was a friendly little boy called Bob. Bob loved to learn about her new toy bear. He would sit in it and think about how it would be a fun game.\nOne day, Bob went to the park with his mommy. He took the toy bear out of the car and told his mommy about the big, soft bear. His mommy gave him the bear a big hug and said, \"I knew you could find your toy bear, but you must be alert and not to give up.\" Bob was very excited and went home.\nBobby asked his mommy, \"Can I play with your bear, please?\" His mommy smiled and said, \"Yes, Bob! You can play with my bear.\" They played together and had lots of fun. The happy bear was very happy too"
